1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Why the Irish hate the British, simple enough for a kid to understand.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,680
It didn't start with one thing. It built over 800 years.

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:12,880
Britain invaded Ireland in the 12th century, took the land, gave it to English settlers.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:16,960
Irish people became tenants on land their families had farmed for generations.

5
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:22,640
Then came the penal laws. Irish Catholics couldn't vote, couldn't own land, couldn't hold public

6
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:27,280
office, couldn't practice their religion openly, couldn't speak their own language in court.

7
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,960
Being Irish was made illegal in your own country. Then the famine hit,

8
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:35,200
1845. One million dead, another million fled.

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:40,000
Britain controlled Ireland's food supply and kept exporting grain while people starved in the

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,640
streets. Irish children watched food leave their country on ships while their families died.

11
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:50,880
In 1916 the Irish rebelled. Britain executed the leaders publicly, one by one.

12
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:56,480
It turned moderates into revolutionaries overnight. Ireland finally won independence in 1922,

13
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:02,160
but Britain kept the north. That partition split families, communities, and cities.

14
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:08,000
It led to decades of bombings and assassinations that didn't end until 1998. 800 years of

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,760
invasion, starvation, and partition. That's why. And that's just one story inside Paladin.

16
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:18,480
It's like Duolingo, but for history lovers. Addictive, smart, surprisingly fun.

17
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:21,360
Try it now and become the most intelligent person in the room.

